; Text in, one ASCII character a card, ended by -1, twice over (the host deals the text a second time); out the
; words, numbers and punctuation. The first time through it only looks for a small letter, and sends 1 if there is
; one (the text is not all capitals), else 0. The second time each character comes with its row of the ASCII
; table after it (the host fetches it by the character's code): its class and value, 1 a capital, 2 a small letter, 3 an
; apostrophe (part of a word); 4 a digit; 5 punctuation; 0 anything else. A word goes out as its letters' codes,
; then -10, then 1 if it has a small letter, else 0; a number as its digits, 500 + d, then -12; punctuation as its
; card (-2 to -5). Then -9.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            p1      INP   c        03-14: the first time: any small letter
  04                    CLA   c
  05                    TAC   p1e
  06                    SUB   c97
  07                    TAC   p1
  08                    SUB   c26
  09                    TAC   low
  10                    JMP   p1
  11            low     CLA   00
  12                    STO   lowt
  13                    JMP   p1
  14            p1e     OUT   lowt
  15            p2      INP   c        15-26: the second time: a character, and its class
  16                    CLA   c
  17                    TAC   fin
  18            gc      INP   cls
  19            gv      INP   val
  20                    CLA   cls
  21                    SUB   00
  22                    TAC   gap
  23                    SUB   n3
  24                    TAC   let
  25                    SUB   00
  26                    TAC   dig
  27                    JMP   close    27-31: punctuation: the token ends, the card goes out
  28                    OUT   val
  29                    JMP   p2
  30            gap     JMP   close
  31                    JMP   p2
  32            dig     CLA   mode     32-43: a digit: a word ends; the number goes on
  33                    SUB   n2
  34                    TAC   dg
  35                    JMP   dout
  36            dg      JMP   close
  37                    CLA   n2
  38                    STO   mode
  39            dout    CLA   val
  40                    ADD   c500
  41                    STO   x
  42                    OUT   x
  43                    JMP   p2
  44            let     CLA   mode     44-63: a letter or apostrophe: a number ends; the word goes on
  45                    SUB   00
  46                    TAC   ws
  47                    SUB   00
  48                    TAC   wout
  49                    JMP   close
  50            ws      CLA   00
  51                    STO   mode
  52                    CLA   z
  53                    STO   lw
  54            wout    OUT   val
  55                    CLA   cls
  56                    SUB   n2
  57                    TAC   p2
  58                    SUB   00
  59                    TAC   slw
  60                    JMP   p2
  61            slw     CLA   00
  62                    STO   lw
  63                    JMP   p2
  64            fin     JMP   close    64-66: the end
  65                    OUT   m9
  66                    HRS   00
  67            close   CLA   99       67-96: a word or a number ends
  68                    STO   ret
  69                    CLA   mode
  70                    SUB   00
  71                    TAC   ret
  72                    SUB   00
  73                    TAC   cw
  74                    OUT   m12
  75                    JMP   cz
  76            cw      OUT   m10
  77                    OUT   lw
  78            cz      CLA   z
  79                    STO   mode
  80            ret     DATA  0
  81            c       DATA  0
  82            cls     DATA  0
  83            val     DATA  0
  84            mode    DATA  0
  85            lw      DATA  0
  86            lowt    DATA  0
  87            x       DATA  0
  88            z       DATA  0
  89            n2      DATA  2
  90            n3      DATA  3
  91            c97     DATA  97
  92            c26     DATA  26
  93            c500    DATA  500
  94            m9      DATA  -9
  95            m10     DATA  -10
  96            m12     DATA  -12
